# Build-context excludes for the dogfood deploy (repo-root context: CI runs
# `docker buildx build -f dogfood/deploy/Dockerfile[.base] .`, so THIS file is the
# one Docker applies — no manual copy step). Without it the context is 3GB+ AND a
# stale local-arch wasmex.so gets baked → boot crash. Single source of truth:
# dogfood/deploy/dockerignore was a drifting duplicate and has been removed.
.git
.claude
constellation
web
desktop
reactor
ether
nexus/_build
nexus/deps
nexus/compilers
nexus/compilers-dist
nexus/wasm-video
nexus/build
nexus/kits
nexus/erl_crash.dump
nexus/.elixir_ls
nexus/vendor/wasmex/priv/native
tiny-lasers/_build
tiny-lasers/deps
tiny-lasers/compilers
tiny-lasers/test
**/target
**/node_modules
**/*.dets
**/*.so
**/*.dylib
**/.DS_Store

# studio SOURCE — only the built swap (dogfood/cloud/demo.html + assets) is served at runtime
dogfood/cloud/studio

# runtime residue that must never enter the image: local Store DB + its SQLite WAL/SHM sidecars,
# and empty ws_* workspace-provisioning leftovers from local runs.
dogfood/.nexus
dogfood/ws_*
